First, we need to determine how many video games Brian had *before* he lost any. Before the loss, Brian had 20 + 5 = 25 video games.

Next, we need to calculate how many video games Bobby has. Bobby has 5 fewer than 3 times as many as Brian, who currently has 20. So Bobby has (3 * 20) - 5 = 60 - 5 = 55 video games.

\boxed{55}

